# One file per page of the settings window.
#
# ⚠️ THE TEN BECAME TWENTY-FIVE AND ARE NOW SEVENTEEN. The split happened
# because Appearance carried 55 rows and System 43 — two pages holding two
# thirds of every setting, each a long list with no structure. "alles
# unübersichtlich und echt schlecht" was about those two. The cut back to
# seventeen is his, and it is the opposite motion for the opposite reason:
# eight pages held settings nobody changes, so their defaults are fixed now
# and the pages are gone. AppearancePage is the one merge among them.
#
# ⚠️ The last four needed NEW keys — `clock`, `motion`, `media` and `lock` did
# not exist in shell.json at all — and every one of those keys was given a real
# reader in the same change. A row over a key nothing reads is a control you can
# move that does nothing, and the audit found five of those.
#
# ⚠️ `NotifyPage`, not `NotificationsPage`: the island already has a page by that
# name, and two QML types with one name in two folders resolve correctly and
# read as a mistake forever after.
#
# Registered here because quickshell loads through a virtual filesystem — see
# ../../common/qmldir.
BarIslandPage 1.0 BarIslandPage.qml
AppearancePage 1.0 AppearancePage.qml
SoundPage 1.0 SoundPage.qml
NotifyPage 1.0 NotifyPage.qml
LockPage 1.0 LockPage.qml
PowerPage 1.0 PowerPage.qml
ColoursPage 1.0 ColoursPage.qml
WallpaperSettingsPage 1.0 WallpaperSettingsPage.qml
AppThemingPage 1.0 AppThemingPage.qml
KeyboardPage 1.0 KeyboardPage.qml
KeysPage 1.0 KeysPage.qml
PointingPage 1.0 PointingPage.qml
WindowsPage 1.0 WindowsPage.qml
ProgramsPage 1.0 ProgramsPage.qml
MachinePage 1.0 MachinePage.qml
# ⚠️ THE TWENTY-SECOND, and the first page whose controls are not SettingRows.
# `outputs` is one object per monitor, so no dotted path names "the refresh rate
# of DP-2" — it is the exemption tests/setting-rows.sh already carries, spent
# here instead of on Size & Shape.
DisplaysPage 1.0 DisplaysPage.qml
